			OSQL
	      ORACLE Visual SQL Query Tool

---------------------------------------------------------------
		     PL/SQL Tool
---------------------------------------------------------------

%%hyperhelp_mark Intro%%
PL/SQL TOOL LAYOUT
---------------------

PL/SQL WINDOW

  -Title Bar-
  There may be any number of PL/SQL windows brought up using
  the "%%hyperhelp_link "Execute PL/SQL..." Osql.menu Options%%" item in the "DB Options" menu of the
  main application window.  Each PL/SQL tool window is titled
  "PL/SQL Window #x", where x is a unique instance number  for
  the current Osql session.

  -Menu Bar-
  Each PL/SQL window has a %%hyperhelp_link "menu bar" Osql.plsql_menu%% with the following menu
  buttons:

  	%%hyperhelp_link " File " Osql.plsql_menu File%%

  	%%hyperhelp_link " Help " Osql.plsql_menu Help%%

  -Button Bar-
  The next frame of the PL/SQL window contains a button,
  "Execute PL/SQL", which, when pressed, causes the code entered
  in the PL/SQL text entry area to be executed.

  If a PL/SQL file has been loaded or saved using the menu
  options, the name of the current save file is shown to the
  right of the "Execute PL/SQL" button.

